# ==============================================================================
# CESIUM PRODUCTION ENVIRONMENT CONFIGURATION (Phase 14)
# ==============================================================================
# This template defines required production environment variables for deploying
# Cesium to Cloudflare Pages/Workers with a hosted Supabase PostgreSQL project.
#
# CRITICAL SECURITY DIRECTIVES:
# 1. NEVER commit production .env or .env.production files to version control.
# 2. NEVER supply SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY to client builds.
# 3. Only supply public anonymous keys (VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY).
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Supabase Production API (Client-Safe)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# In Cloudflare Pages Dashboard: Settings -> Environment Variables -> Production
# Or via wrangler secret / GitHub Actions Secrets:
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://<your-production-project-id>.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Node & Deployment Target Environment
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NODE_ENV=production
NITRO_PRESET=cloudflare-module

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Production Supabase Security Checklist
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ensure the following in Supabase Project Settings:
# - Auth -> URL Configuration:
#     Site URL: https://<your-custom-domain>.com
#     Redirect URLs: https://<your-custom-domain>.com/**
# - Database -> Realtime:
#     Verify 'messages' table is published to supabase_realtime.
# - Storage -> Buckets:
#     Verify 'public_assets' bucket is created and RLS policies applied.
# - Network Restrictions:
#     Enforce SSL/TLS connections (pg_stat_ssl).
# ==============================================================================
